Mark Healey <die@spammer.die> wrote:
>I got a big box of stuff that I can't use for various reasons (don't
>know what it is, out of charges, cursed, etc).  I've been humping it
>down about 5 levels when I go about that much deeper.  Right now it is
>on level 16 and I've explored down to 20.  Not knowing how deep these
>dungeons go, I'm wondering if I should keep bringing it down.  I'm
>wasting a lot of food going back and fourth for these trips.

Don't bother. Later in the game it's much easier to nip up and down
yourself to deal with inventory; you don't need to haul your whole stash
around with you. If you're going to die for lack of something (other
than food), it'll be because you don't have it on your person rather
than because you don't have it five levels closer.

Do try to identify as much as you can as quickly as you can, one way or
another. I find it useful to carry a sample of a number of unidentified
items with me in case I get the opportunity to do that, assuming I can
do so without becoming burdened.

